{:edb/db-before-t 2469 :edb/db-after-t 2470 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535782 50 #inst "2026-10-09T07:09:10.994Z" 13194139535782 true] [17592186161913 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366056 13194139535782 true] [17592186161914 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366063 13194139535782 true] [17592186161915 1020 #edb/ref 17592186366070 13194139535782 true] [17592186162517 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535782 true] [17592186162517 1100 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139535782 true] [17592186162517 1100 "$\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x, y) = x_{1}y_{1} - 3x_{1}y_{3} + x_{2}y_{3} - x_{3}y_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a + b + c$?" 13194139535782 false] [17592186162517 1145 "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+1+(-1)=1.\n$$" 13194139535782 true] [17592186162540 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535782 true] [17592186162540 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139535782 true] [17592186162540 1100 "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form $x^{T}Ay$ in terms of the components of $x = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $y = \\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$?" 13194139535782 false] [17592186162540 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(3){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ -3{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-3{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366056 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366057 13194139535782 true] [17592186366056 1089 "q-140853" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366056 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535782 true] [17592186366056 1100 "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366056 1113 #uuid "ac50817d-d0cd-5bab-aa46-bd534774fa22" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366056 1145 "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =30+6-15+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366058 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366059 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366060 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366061 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366062 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1041 "selection" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366060 13194139535782 true] [17592186366057 1110 #uuid "5aa60481-686a-5eb6-ac2e-42effa99d225" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366058 1034 "11" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535782 true] [17592186366058 1111 #uuid "b2ebb4f8-da81-590f-b864-dcd9284598cd" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366059 1034 "16" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535782 true] [17592186366059 1111 #uuid "ba0f3095-cf7b-5d71-9a79-e3b700e224d2" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366060 1034 "21" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535782 true] [17592186366060 1111 #uuid "3fc25b48-e112-5f68-8e77-6f57099aeb50" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366061 1034 "42" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535782 true] [17592186366061 1111 #uuid "55ae36c2-2d7f-533c-ba1f-473ff3462994" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366062 1034 "18" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366062 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535782 true] [17592186366062 1111 #uuid "aa86bd07-88ac-5bdb-8039-5173c1cc21c5" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366063 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366064 13194139535782 true] [17592186366063 1089 "q-93982" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366063 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535782 true] [17592186366063 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366063 1113 #uuid "95bc1c5a-4cad-5587-8969-cf8149e63588" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366063 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ -{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535782 true] [17592186366064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366065 13194139535782 true] [17592186366064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366066 13194139535782 true] [17592186366064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366067 13194139535782 true] [17592186366064 1000 #edb/